Hi Waqas,

I don't follow SEAT, and don't know this document or discussion, but I do u=
nderstand the IETF process rules pretty well.

At that first data tracker link you provided you will see:

"This document is an Internet-Draft (I-D). Anyone may submit an I-D to the =
IETF. This I-D is not endorsed by the IETF and has no formal standing in th=
e IETF standards process<https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc2026/>."

Unless the SEAT WG has adopted the document (and hence the name of the draf=
t changes to draft-ietf-seat-early-attestation, then this is NOT an IETF do=
cument and hence it is incorrect to say that the SEAT WG is "working on it"=
.  The only status that this draft has is that it is an idea from a set of =
authors which they would like the SEAT WG to consider.  Anyone can submit a=
 draft for consideration by the WG.  Perhaps the authors will consider your=
 patch, perhaps they won't.  It is up to them since they are currently sole=
ly responsible for the document, not the SEAT WG, nor the IETF.

Also worth seeing https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-wkumari-not-a-draf=
t/.

Kind regards,
Rob


