Cc: ietf@ietf.org <ietf@ietf.org>; tls@ietf.org <tls@ietf.org>; ietf-discus=
sion@listi.jpberlin.de <ietf-discussion@listi.jpberlin.de>
Subject: Re: [TLS] NSA / IETF Discussion List

Dear Ken Kubota,
IETF has SEAT working group. It works on TLS 1.3 extension. SEAT has https:=
//datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-fossati-seat-early-attestation/.
41 high class CVEs were filed against it: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/=
draft-intra-handshake-fail/
They also provided patch to fix. The patch was never applied.
Anyone who talks about CVEs is given "official warning" by chairs.
Is it in scope of your mailing list https://listi.jpberlin.de/mailman/listi=
nfo/ietf-discussion?
Thanks,
Waqas


On Wed, Oct 14, 2026 at 12:14 PM Ken Kubota <ietf@kenkubota.de> wrote:
For those who disagree with NSA activities at the IETF or wish to find solu=
tions for the issues concerning the current IETF situation, you can join th=
is mailing list:

https://listi.jpberlin.de/mailman/listinfo/ietf-discussion


Kind regards,

Ken Kubota

____________________________________________________

Ken Kubota
https://doi.org/10.4444/100
_______________________________________________
TLS mailing list -- tls@ietf.org
To unsubscribe send an email to tls-leave@ietf.org

